Kaggriculture, team 42 (Kefei Yan, Frank Yang, yirenw11)
https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/kaggriculture

This repository holds the team's write-up, its own tools and research code, and the agents it ran on the
leaderboard. Those agents are derivative works of the public "cha22 agent" by Abhinav0370
(https://www.kaggle.com/code/abhinav0370/cha22-agent, main.py SHA-256 127ed3e6...), itself an Apache-2.0
derivative of the public route-replay lineage (thomastschinkel, yhay81, destbreso, aurax7, tetsutani,
prvsiyan, Dmitrii Gluzdov, Ahmed Berat Ozer and others); v3 is built on Dmitrii Gluzdov's public rescue agent
of the same lineage. Every package under submissions/ embeds its base source (verbatim up to v9; from v10 on
with the production patches listed in that package's own NOTICE.txt), keeps all upstream license text and
attribution notices, and carries its own LICENSE.txt and NOTICE.txt.

The wheat tick-arbitrage idea behind the TICK layer was learned from public replays of the team Otter Vibe.

